        "findings": {
          "sameWorkPackageSerialization": "Shared::ServiceContext#in_mutex_context wraps SetAttributesService (UpdateContract) + WorkPackage#save + Journal write inside OpenProject::Mutex.with_advisory_lock_transaction(model) (`mutex_on_WorkPackage_<id>`) plus ActiveRecord optimistic locking (`WHERE id = $1 AND lock_version = $2`). Concurrent mutations on the SAME WorkPackage row serialize atomically.",
          "crossEntityReadCommittedGap": "As documented in lib/open_project/mutex.rb, PostgreSQL runs at READ COMMITTED isolation and the advisory lock keys only on `mutex_on_WorkPackage_<id>`. Plain SELECTs in UpdateContract against separate tables (`member_roles`, `workflows`, `versions`, or a separate parent/approval WorkPackage) do NOT lock those rows; concurrent revocations on separate entities between validate and COMMIT are not blocked without explicit row/advisory locking.",
          "specificTermsApprovalVersionBinding": "If human-approved terms live on the target WorkPackage row itself, any revoke-or-edit bumps `work_packages.lock_version`, so binding `lockVersion: v_approved` rejects ABA re-approvals under altered terms (`409`). If human-approved terms live on a separate entity/row, stock UpdateContract does NOT bind that entity's version or terms digest—requiring an atomic validator/gateway checking `(approval_id, approval_lock_version, terms_sha256)`.",
          "lostAckOperationBindingContract": "Stock OpenProject has no native Idempotency-Key header on PATCH /api/v3/work_packages/{id}, and WorkPackagePayloadRepresenter ignores `journalNotes` / `comment` on PATCH (comments live on separate non-atomic POST /activities). Furthermore, under default `Setting.journal_aggregation_time_minutes = 5`, `Journals::CreateService#aggregatable?` coalesces consecutive unmarked PATCHes by the SAME user into one journal row (advancing `work_packages.lock_version` faster than `journals.version` and overwriting `work_package_journals` in place). Therefore: (1) API `/activities` alone without DB `work_package_journals` returns `unknown` on a dropped-ack PATCH; (2) embedding `<!-- opbind-v1:<sha256> -->` in `description.raw` binds the exact operation in `work_package_journals.description` across immediate reads and cross-user overwrites (`committed`), while honestly degrading to `unknown` if a same-user edit within the aggregation window overwrote the snapshot; (3) blind retries on a bumped `lockVersion` are always forbidden.",
          "mockVsRealProbeBoundary": "Loopback mock tests establish runner and reconciler logic only (`establishesUpstreamAppContract: false`); only running `probeOpenProjectDualRelease` against live OpenProject 13.4.0 and 14.0.0 releases establishes the upstream application contract."
        }
      },
